    "detailed_description": "<h2 id=\"system-architecture\">System Architecture</h2>\n<p>Built on Arduino MKR WiFi 1010 with TCA9548A I2C multiplexer managing three magnetometers sharing the same address. The system uses PlatformIO development environment with libraries including WiFiNINA, ArduinoJson, and PubSubClient for MQTT. A rolling average algorithm cleans inconsistent magnetometer readings, and an enumerated switching method rotates between I2C channels while conserving memory.</p>\n<h2 id=\"key-features\">Key Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>LED Node Selection:</em> Rotary encoder dial selects specific LED nodes on the wall</li>\n<li><em>Color Control:</em> Three TLV493D magnetometers (Red, Green, Blue) measure magnet distance from a wand to generate RGB values (0-255)</li>\n<li><em>Visual Feedback:</em> SSD1306 OLED display provides user interface information</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"technical-challenges\">Technical Challenges</h2>\n<p>Magnetometer Range: TLV493D sensors only detect magnetic disturbance within 3-4cm, causing abrupt color transitions rather than smooth gradients. Future improvements include stronger magnetometers with adjustable I2C addresses to eliminate the multiplexer and improve reading speed and consistency.</p>",
