    "detailed_description": "<h2 id=\"system-architecture\">System Architecture</h2>\n<p>Hardware consists of Arduino Nano 33 BLE, three flex sensors with 47.5kΩ pull-up resistors, and PCB terminal blocks. The system uses 3.3V power (not 5V) due to laptop USB power limitations. Software uses Edge Impulse CLI&#39;s edge-impulse-data-forwarder tool to stream sensor data for training. The Arduino script reads analog values from flex sensors and outputs to serial for data collection.</p>\n<h2 id=\"key-features\">Key Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Gesture Detection:</em> Three flex sensors capture finger movements for gesture recognition</li>\n<li><em>Edge ML Training:</em> Edge Impulse platform enables custom model training for specific gestures</li>\n<li><em>Real-time Processing:</em> Arduino Nano 33 BLE processes sensor readings in real-time</li>\n<li><em>Deployment Ready:</em> Trained models can be deployed directly to embedded devices</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"technical-challenges\">Technical Challenges</h2>\n<p>Training Optimization: Best results achieved by setting 10-second sample times, performing gestures slowly, then using Edge Impulse&#39;s split sample feature to generate multiple training samples rapidly from single recordings, improving model accuracy efficiently.</p>",
