    "detailed_description": "<h2 id=\"system-architecture\">System Architecture</h2>\n<p>An Arduino Uno processes sensor data and displays results on a 7-segment display. An ESP32-S3 module receives serial data at 9600 baud and transmits via MQTT. Python scripts collect data, merge sessions, and perform statistical analysis including ANOVA testing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"key-features\">Key Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Hardware:</em> Arduino Uno, ESP32, ultrasonic transducers, 7-segment display</li>\n<li><em>Output:</em> JSON format with wind speed (m/s) and direction (0-360°)</li>\n<li><em>Calibration:</em> Three-point system using still air and known wind conditions (9 m/s reference)</li>\n<li><em>Manufacturing:</em> CAD files for 3D printing and laser cutting, plus detailed assembly instructions</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"technical-challenges\">Technical Challenges</h2>\n<p>The system addresses calibration accuracy through user-updatable constants, ensures reliable cross-platform communication with standardized protocols, and maintains security by isolating credentials in separate files. Python utilities streamline data collection across multiple sessions.\nThe project integrates embedded systems, wireless networking, and data analysis into a complete meteorological instrument suitable for education and research applications.</p>",
    "created_at": "2025-11-12T01:21:47.651307+00:00",
