    "detailed_description": "<h2 id=\"system-architecture\">System Architecture</h2>\n<p>Built on ESP8266 Node MCU with PlatformIO. Hardware includes FQP30N06L MOSFET controlling heating pads, capacitive sensor for touch detection, and Neopixel LEDs. Each device requires unique MAC address configuration and calibrated touch threshold values stored in <code>macAddr.h</code>. 3D-printed enclosure houses protoboard circuit with translucent bottom for LED diffusion. Power supplied via USB cable.</p>\n<h2 id=\"key-features\">Key Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Warmth Transfer:</em> Heating pads create warm sensations triggered by partner&#39;s touch</li>\n<li><em>Capacitive Touch Detection:</em> Aluminum foil sensor with 220kΩ resistor detects hand placement</li>\n<li><em>ESP-NOW Communication:</em> Direct device-to-device communication via ESP8266 Node MCU</li>\n<li><em>Deployment Ready:</em> Trained models can be deployed directly to embedded devices</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"technical-challenges\">Technical Challenges</h2>\n<p>Future Development: Planned improvements include material research, exploring NiChrome wire heating elements, PCB conversion from prototype board, migrating from ESP-NOW to WiFi connectivity, and adding QR/NFC pairing for easier multi-device setup and WiFi configuration.</p>",
    "created_at": "2025-11-12T22:47:49.901547+00:00",
